# EBC APP — TypeScript & React

Full doc: `docs/engineering/standards/coding.md`

## TypeScript

- `strict: true`; no `any` at boundaries
- String unions / `as const` — not TS enums
- `import type` for type-only imports
- Explicit return types on exported functions

## React / Next.js

- Server Components default; `'use client'` only when needed
- Props types in `*.types.ts` when non-trivial
- Extract hooks to `use-*.ts` in the same feature folder
- Handle loading | empty | error | success for data views

## Imports order

1. External packages
2. `@/` aliases (barrels only for cross-folder)
3. Relative (within feature)
4. `import type`

## Do not

- Put business logic in `page.tsx` or presentational components
- Use `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` without security review
- `console.log` member or giving data
- Default-export components (Next.js pages excepted)
